{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender offset edge loop cut blender offset edge loop cut","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut.md","fileName":"Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:18\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Mesh Modeling and Modifiers]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Mesh Modeling and Modifiers","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender offset edge loop cut blender offset edge loop cut","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut.md","fileName":"Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut","heading":"Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Offset Edge Loop Cut creates parallel loops on either side of an existing edge loop. The paired cuts add a controllable band of topology around a feature rather than inserting only one loop through the surrounding faces.\n\nThe new support edges can sharpen a subdivision result, frame an inset region, or reserve topology for later shaping. Their spacing should match the intended silhouette because closely packed loops create a tighter transition.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Mesh Modeling and Modifiers","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Offset Edge Loop Cut.md::2","sourceKey":"6